<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kangaba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kangaba is a region on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali">Mali</a>, the original heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keita-dynasty">Keita dynasty</a>. As the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> declined, the Keita rulers lost their wider territories. By 1500 they retained only the Kangaba heartland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kangaba.jpg" alt="Kangaba" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Sessoms · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entrance_to_Kangaba.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
